      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Reports have been weighted since the implementation of the safety system. I've had this information from the VRC team themselves and don't have a source to link to unfortunately.\nAutomated banning is a bad idea, the nuisance rank already exist and keeps troublemakers away from public instances and muted unless you manually override them.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-12-18T20:28:54.789Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "As many of us know, reporting players does not yield much of a visible result. I actively report toxic users but sometimes feel that my actions don't have much of an impact.\nSuggestion: I believe all reports should not be created equal. Reports submitted by newer or even harmful/toxic players should not be as 'trusted' or heavily weighted as reports by trusted users (or even hidden veteran/legendary/staff users).\nThey should make the banning system more automated so that it does not fall directly onto the moderation team. They can only keep up with so much, and they have their own bias and perspectives.\nWhen multiple high rank players report a user, a temp ban (depending on cumulative reports and/or bans) should be reasonable.\nThere would, no doubt, be users abusing this system. Users found to frequently submit false reports should have their credibility or ranking decreased accordingly.",
